113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 88 0 R
/T (Incident records often require consistent and accurate data entry to ensure effective triage, routing, and resolution. However, relying solely on user awareness and manual checks can lead to incomplete, inconsistent, or incorrect data being submitted. This can impact reporting accuracy, SLA compliance, and overall service quality. To address this challenge, there is a need to enforce conditional field behavior and validation directly at the user interface level. Implementing standardized UI Policies and Client Scripts helps control field visibility, mandatory status, and save-time validation, ensuring that Incident records meet defined business rules before they are submitted.)
/E (Incident records often require consistent and accurate data entry to ensure effective triage, routing, and resolution. However, relying solely on user awareness and manual checks can lead to incomplete, inconsistent, or incorrect data being submitted. This can impact reporting accuracy, SLA compliance, and overall service quality. To address this challenge, there is a need to enforce conditional field behavior and validation directly at the user interface level. Implementing standardized UI Policies and Client Scripts helps control field visibility, mandatory status, and save-time validation, ensuring that Incident records meet defined business rules before they are submitted.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
